{"name":"Snowmelt","hex":"#c9e6e9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snowmelt","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Runoff from melting snow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowmelt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snowmelt","blocks":[{"text":"In hydrology, snowmelt is surface runoff produced from melting snow. It can also be used to describe the period or season during which such runoff is produced. Water produced by snowmelt is an important part of the annual water cycle in many parts of the world, in some cases contributing high fractions of the annual runoff in a watershed. Predicting snowmelt runoff from a drainage basin may be a part of designing water control projects. Rapid snowmelt can cause flooding. If the snowmelt is then frozen, very dangerous conditions and accidents can occur, introducing the need for salt to melt the ice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Timelapse_of_Winter%27s_End_at_Bertram_Creek_Park_overlooking_Okanagan_Lake%2C_includes_Snowmelt%2C_Sunset_and_Venus_Set.webm/330px--Timelapse_of_Winter%27s_End_at_Bertram_Creek_Park_overlooking_Okanagan_Lake%2C_includes_Snowmelt%2C_Sunset_and_Venus_Set.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowmelt","wikidata":"Q1754697"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Vegetation_Induced_Circular_Snowmelt.jpg/500px-Vegetation_Induced_Circular_Snowmelt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Vegetation_Induced_Circular_Snowmelt.jpg/1280px-Vegetation_Induced_Circular_Snowmelt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Vegetation_Induced_Circular_Snowmelt.jpg/500px-Vegetation_Induced_Circular_Snowmelt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vegetation gi